{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/comments.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:44.760936Z","id":"9eef4d082e1340313ba1ff2060144c7879d3e08dd7b19e14edcd8aa7a283a10c","body":{"detail":"onWorking sets `offWorking` (the clax:event listener) and adds `fn` to `workingFns` before it awaits `rpc.call(\"comments\", \"watchWorking\", [])` (lines 226-229). That call can reject: the shell's handler (web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts:552-557) awaits `loadWorking()`, a lazy chunk, and throws `closed()` once disposed. On a rejection the page's promise rejects, so it never receives the unsubscriber, yet `fn` stays in `workingFns` and `offWorking` stays non-null. Every later onWorking then takes the `else` branch (line 230), calls `working()` once and never asks the shell to watch, so no later change is ever pushed: clax-extensions.d.ts:71 promises `fn` is called 'on every change'. bridge/test/comments.test.ts:156-163 covers only the success path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":223},"end":{"line":241},"content_hash":"06d8066f349fd347bdb88b19cf993e41bd566c0f109fc74b0d537b6f7ac68ef0"},"suggested_fix":"Await watchWorking inside try/catch; on failure remove `f` from `workingFns` and, when the set is empty, call `offWorking()` and set it back to null before rethrowing. A test with a shell whose watchWorking rejects once, then succeeds, checks that the second onWorking subscribes again.","summary":"A failed watchWorking leaves comments.onWorking broken for the rest of the page: offWorking stays set, so no later onWorking subscribes again","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/comments.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:16.139865Z","id":"0749ad2fedd9ac352a6ca39fd4e5f25e4aee64b0aa8fed5dcc205d9706f021ee","body":{"detail":"web/bridge/src/caps/comments.ts:226-229 adds f and assigns offWorking before `await rpc.call(\"comments\", \"watchWorking\", [])` with no try/catch; a rejection propagates without undoing either. Line 230 then routes every later call to the `else` branch (one `working()` read, no watchWorking). The shell's handler can throw: web/shell/src/caps/comments.ts:552-557 (`await loadWorking(); if (disposed) throw closed();`), and without watchWorking set the shell never pushes (watchingWorking stays false). web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts:71 promises calls 'on every change'. web/bridge/test/comments.test.ts:150-164 tests only the success path. Kind concern is right.","kind":"comment","references":"9eef4d082e1340313ba1ff2060144c7879d3e08dd7b19e14edcd8aa7a283a10c","summary":"confirmed: a rejected watchWorking leaves offWorking set and fn in workingFns, so no later onWorking subscribes","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/comments.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:24:50.629541Z","id":"bac71626df8071313fd7d54701ebdaabc9a3df72c941896dcdcb7211f2cf579e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:53274912a","summary":"Fixed: onWorking shares one watch promise and tears down on refusal so the next call watches again; web/bridge/test/comments.test.ts refused-watch case passes.","supersedes":"9eef4d082e1340313ba1ff2060144c7879d3e08dd7b19e14edcd8aa7a283a10c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:10:35.284096Z","id":"e81b5fc186c9ccf9203ac9aa92ad8fe7756b8d831a48f94177976af1b9536a46","body":{"detail":"/_clax/api/ (crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_api.rs) serves no event stream, so dbTransport learns of other writers' changes only from a framing Clax shell (db/changed after db.watch, web/shell/src/caps/db.ts) or by polling at UNWATCHED_POLL_MS. A world-open site with many visitors costs one read per subscription per visitor every 5 s, and their onSnapshot lags others' writes by up to 5 s; framed, the shell's reports make it immediate.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":77},"content_hash":"bd9d72cbb400d65344d813048c6eb39892658f81c2fc4d1cbde493a8a47c104b"},"suggested_fix":"Serve the artifact's doc events on the site host (an SSE route or frames on the /_clax/api/room socket, filtered by the caller's db level as the public host's stream is), and let dbTransport follow it in place of the poll.","summary":"A page opened directly on its site refetches every db subscription every 5 s: the site API has no change stream","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/resolve.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:10:35.284153Z","id":"16431b8250c0c56886ef9c0bbff26b3ca8386dd1655f666a9fe61aef2ecce26d","body":{"detail":"artifact.publish posts /api/artifacts/<id>/versions with the owner's token after the shell's strict gesture tier (web/shell/src/caps/artifact.ts, frameGestureStrict in web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts). The site API serves no versions route, and a gesture check in the bridge would share the page's realm, so the page could publish on any click of its own. Moving publish to the site means a versions route on /_clax/api/ and a decision on what gesture rule a top-level page gets.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":26},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"24247bd6018c97dbb6d33e67045c958889bc886c43b8551ffeebfa3d93de2f6c"},"summary":"The artifact capability stays the framing shell's: top-level, use(\"artifact\") resolves null","tags":["site-origins","status:needs-decision","revisit:a page opened directly on its site must publish its own versions","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:10:35.284192Z","id":"f9fbffd31c9b90a2bd72c394a20468f971acddbe601b88b1366693a6998cd205","body":{"detail":"The site API serves whoami but no viewers' names (no /api/viewers on /_clax/api/), so userLocals answers profiles with the viewer's own name and \"\" for every other ID, and search with [], unless a framing Clax shell serves user (then web/shell/src/caps/user.ts looks them up). A top-level page that shows room peers or document authors by name shows them unnamed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":258},"end":{"line":310},"content_hash":"b76040f0363cb9ff61856d5da4c3daa7c401a53ffd32c99b173382f69e1c6022"},"suggested_fix":"A /_clax/api/viewers?ids= route answering the names the caller's level may see, for the bridge to call in place of the shell.","summary":"user.profiles and user.search on a page opened directly on its site name only the viewer and find no one","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:10:35.284255Z","id":"988af87ba9545233084c02b242ffc781d696bd0dc7636a3ff160919f61eb7ff6","body":{"detail":"originUse calls location.origin's /_clax/api/, which only a site host serves (crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_api.rs). A local shell with no site origins frames /c/<id>/v/<n>/ on the main origin, sandboxed (web/shell/src/origin.ts, docs/contract.md); there the declaration read fails (404, or new URL(\"null\") throws) and those capabilities resolve null where the shell used to serve them. The shell framing every artifact on its site origin (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md Task 5) removes that mode.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":46},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"57f7d6b7ad3d54c8a0acbea11b7acd5079eb15cf7743936c4292e5d52b818a66"},"summary":"A page served outside its site host (/c/<id>/v/<n>/, or a sandboxed opaque-origin frame) resolves db, assets, user and room null","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:11:53.288793Z","id":"baa4014bf0c6e17d98d43c7d03427d73d2aec917d8bdefb22ee1e37c37336fa6","body":{"detail":"/_clax/api/ (crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_api.rs) serves no event stream, so dbTransport learns of other writers' changes only from a framing Clax shell (db/changed after db.watch, web/shell/src/caps/db.ts) or by polling: UNWATCHED_POLL_MS 5 s after a change, the page's own write, a focus or coming back into view, then 10, 20 and 30 s while nothing changes, none while the page is hidden. Each poll's reads send their last ETag back and an unchanged one is the site's 304 (docs_tag in site_api.rs, keyed on the artifact's document sequence), so a quiet poll costs a sequence lookup per read; a top-level page still sees another writer's change up to 30 s late. A site change stream is the later step.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":71},"end":{"line":79},"content_hash":"c081211fbf3a316ec11790be2eecd3a98ae8bcfe7f8598b291659c5e57869bc1"},"suggested_fix":"Serve the artifact's doc events on the site host (an SSE route or frames on the /_clax/api/room socket, filtered by the caller's db level as the public host's stream is), and let dbTransport follow it in place of the poll.","summary":"A page opened directly on its site polls its db subscriptions: the site API has no change stream","supersedes":"e81b5fc186c9ccf9203ac9aa92ad8fe7756b8d831a48f94177976af1b9536a46","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/resolve.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:11:53.307745Z","id":"41375d441cde3a21dc526287ec8ecc21ecc0a453f5dfb2b8c494c1db4d27f1c5","body":{"detail":"artifact.publish posts /api/artifacts/<id>/versions with the owner's token after the shell's strict gesture tier (web/shell/src/caps/artifact.ts, frameGestureStrict in web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts). The site API serves no versions route, and a gesture check in the bridge would share the page's realm, so the page could publish on any click of its own. Moving publish to the site means a versions route on /_clax/api/ and a decision on what gesture rule a top-level page gets.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":26}},"summary":"The artifact capability stays the framing shell's: top-level, use(\"artifact\") resolves null","supersedes":"16431b8250c0c56886ef9c0bbff26b3ca8386dd1655f666a9fe61aef2ecce26d","tags":["site-origins","status:needs-decision","revisit:a page opened directly on its site must publish its own versions","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:11:53.326320Z","id":"990d31427e97ad9014b980c4fac6a04847d6020f6b498941db24848f33d8c5c0","body":{"detail":"The site API serves whoami but no viewers' names (no /api/viewers on /_clax/api/), so userLocals answers profiles with the viewer's own name and \"\" for every other ID, and search with [], unless a framing Clax shell serves user (then web/shell/src/caps/user.ts looks them up). A top-level page that shows room peers or document authors by name shows them unnamed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":304},"end":{"line":370},"content_hash":"f0681012a59f53638565dc7b484158ebc0329a9f596668d76fb7ce4017cb2031"},"suggested_fix":"A /_clax/api/viewers?ids= route answering the names the caller's level may see, for the bridge to call in place of the shell.","summary":"user.profiles and user.search on a page opened directly on its site name only the viewer and find no one","supersedes":"f9fbffd31c9b90a2bd72c394a20468f971acddbe601b88b1366693a6998cd205","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:11:53.345093Z","id":"7a7d190962d8c07aaccc8c66fbcd750ac4d47531b04f18559c1c80def71ba6e6","body":{"detail":"originUse calls location.origin's /_clax/api/, which only a site host serves (crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_api.rs). A local shell with no site origins frames /c/<id>/v/<n>/ on the main origin, sandboxed (web/shell/src/origin.ts, docs/contract.md); there the declaration read fails (404, or new URL(\"null\") throws) and those capabilities resolve null where the shell used to serve them. The shell framing every artifact on its site origin (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md Task 5) removes that mode.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"57f7d6b7ad3d54c8a0acbea11b7acd5079eb15cf7743936c4292e5d52b818a66"},"summary":"A page served outside its site host (/c/<id>/v/<n>/, or a sandboxed opaque-origin frame) resolves db, assets, user and room null","supersedes":"988af87ba9545233084c02b242ffc781d696bd0dc7636a3ff160919f61eb7ff6","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:34:07.358079Z","id":"58ac50d830b354a21fb58ca5f1afd3c598b9641fcd81a07d90371d2e48475362","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:754dadb3","summary":"Obsolete: the shell frames every artifact on its site origin through a site code, and the sandboxed /c/<id>/v/<n>/ mode is gone (docs/contract.md: the keyed /c/ addresses are 404; the frame has no sandbox attribute). web/e2e/site-runtime.spec.ts's framed spec passes with db and user resolved on the site.","supersedes":"7a7d190962d8c07aaccc8c66fbcd750ac4d47531b04f18559c1c80def71ba6e6","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/room-socket.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:34:07.379594Z","id":"aad80659f9b1a7ccec54d02eca2ab8a558bd331dc211224e09249cae85920411","body":{"detail":"renamed() opens a new socket when the viewer changes, but the site fixes a socket's level by its session's holder (crates/clax-http/src/db_caller.rs site_caller): a guest's and a link viewer's are public, named or not, and a person's follows their name, which an invite always sets (crates/clax-store/src/people.rs create_invite). The holder is the one the site code named when the session was made (crates/clax-http/src/site_access.rs caller_holder reads it from the session row), so a link viewer who names themselves stays the site's link viewer (whoami's id null) until the frame's next handshake. web/e2e/room.spec.ts's hosted guest spec checks only that naming keeps the room connected under the same peer at the public level; the level change is covered by web/bridge/test/room-socket.test.ts alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":149},"end":{"line":161},"content_hash":"a39fc8726aec88133b9ed49ac412db90137c15328cf59e233080da9dbd22dfff"},"summary":"A room reconnect at a new level is reachable by no viewer of a hosted daemon, so no browser test covers it","tags":["site-origins","testing","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:35:36.165117Z","id":"47bf885b8f360265de6c9b90884c0044a28ce8dae19018f515aa02c3075ad2b3","body":{"detail":"/_clax/api/ (crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_api.rs) serves no event stream, so dbTransport learns of other writers' changes only from a framing Clax shell (db/changed after db.watch, web/shell/src/caps/db.ts) or by polling: UNWATCHED_POLL_MS 5 s after a change, the page's own write, a focus or coming back into view, then 10, 20 and 30 s while nothing changes, none while the page is hidden. Each poll's reads send their last ETag back and an unchanged one is the site's 304 (docs_tag in site_api.rs, keyed on the artifact's document sequence), so a quiet poll costs a sequence lookup per read; a top-level page still sees another writer's change up to 30 s late. A site change stream is the later step.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":90},"content_hash":"c081211fbf3a316ec11790be2eecd3a98ae8bcfe7f8598b291659c5e57869bc1"},"suggested_fix":"Serve the artifact's doc events on the site host (an SSE route or frames on the /_clax/api/room socket, filtered by the caller's db level as the public host's stream is), and let dbTransport follow it in place of the poll.","summary":"A page opened directly on its site polls its db subscriptions: the site API has no change stream","supersedes":"baa4014bf0c6e17d98d43c7d03427d73d2aec917d8bdefb22ee1e37c37336fa6","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:35:36.185242Z","id":"f7161bbc3950856f75338ccc7be1f3191b040d553d84c3f8f7629544a6045487","body":{"detail":"The site API serves whoami but no viewers' names (no /api/viewers on /_clax/api/), so userLocals answers profiles with the viewer's own name and \"\" for every other ID, and search with [], unless a framing Clax shell serves user (then web/shell/src/caps/user.ts looks them up). A top-level page that shows room peers or document authors by name shows them unnamed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":315},"end":{"line":381},"content_hash":"f0681012a59f53638565dc7b484158ebc0329a9f596668d76fb7ce4017cb2031"},"suggested_fix":"A /_clax/api/viewers?ids= route answering the names the caller's level may see, for the bridge to call in place of the shell.","summary":"user.profiles and user.search on a page opened directly on its site name only the viewer and find no one","supersedes":"990d31427e97ad9014b980c4fac6a04847d6020f6b498941db24848f33d8c5c0","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:45:48.802223Z","id":"9be550fdbf1d2060a46ba37629ba482ba0b8cc7b86809d74f710212b11d706e7","body":{"detail":"siteOf memoises whoami per document, and user.me(), name(), can() and the db level the page infers read that answer. The framing shell's room/viewer report reconnects the room socket (room-socket.ts renamed) but does not refresh whoami, so a viewer who names themselves keeps the name '' and the old level in user.* until the frame loads another document. web/e2e/user-assets.spec.ts 'user in the owner shell' reads the new name from the next document.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":42},"content_hash":"632ade713a7ace5e1917b3e13bbe4368b99ed7516742c636fee71cb342dcea2a"},"summary":"A page learns who its viewer is from the site once: a rename, a sign-in or a change of rights shows in user.* only from the next document","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:20.664386Z","id":"c955cd989deafa966ae0cc77e579b1ab14a357fdaa809a2f24208a974ff9a2ce","body":{"detail":"/_clax/api/ (crates/clax-server/src/routes/site_api.rs) serves no event stream, so dbTransport learns of other writers' changes only from a framing Clax shell (db/changed after db.watch, web/shell/src/caps/db.ts) or by polling: UNWATCHED_POLL_MS 5 s after a change, the page's own write, a focus or coming back into view, then 10, 20 and 30 s while nothing changes, none while the page is hidden. Each poll's reads send their last ETag back and an unchanged one is the site's 304 (docs_tag in site_api.rs, keyed on the artifact's document sequence), so a quiet poll costs a sequence lookup per read; a top-level page still sees another writer's change up to 30 s late. A site change stream is the later step.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":85},"end":{"line":93},"content_hash":"c081211fbf3a316ec11790be2eecd3a98ae8bcfe7f8598b291659c5e57869bc1"},"suggested_fix":"Serve the artifact's doc events on the site host (an SSE route or frames on the /_clax/api/room socket, filtered by the caller's db level as the public host's stream is), and let dbTransport follow it in place of the poll.","summary":"A page opened directly on its site polls its db subscriptions: the site API has no change stream","supersedes":"47bf885b8f360265de6c9b90884c0044a28ce8dae19018f515aa02c3075ad2b3","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:21.390647Z","id":"1b8d30f5aaa319a37749f6243a08c0c2e05eebf3f6a5d46fe39ffd1f2f929cca","body":{"detail":"The site API serves whoami but no viewers' names (no /api/viewers on /_clax/api/), so userLocals answers profiles with the viewer's own name and \"\" for every other ID, and search with [], unless a framing Clax shell serves user (then web/shell/src/caps/user.ts looks them up). A top-level page that shows room peers or document authors by name shows them unnamed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":401},"end":{"line":467},"content_hash":"f0681012a59f53638565dc7b484158ebc0329a9f596668d76fb7ce4017cb2031"},"suggested_fix":"A /_clax/api/viewers?ids= route answering the names the caller's level may see, for the bridge to call in place of the shell.","summary":"user.profiles and user.search on a page opened directly on its site name only the viewer and find no one","supersedes":"f7161bbc3950856f75338ccc7be1f3191b040d553d84c3f8f7629544a6045487","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:21.821205Z","id":"2afb097412166c983f7d95eb4c236295e18aad58214fac8349d458cc5ae8a112","body":{"detail":"siteOf memoises whoami per document, and user.me(), name(), can() and the db level the page infers read that answer. The framing shell's room/viewer report reconnects the room socket (room-socket.ts renamed) but does not refresh whoami, so a viewer who names themselves keeps the name '' and the old level in user.* until the frame loads another document. web/e2e/user-assets.spec.ts 'user in the owner shell' reads the new name from the next document.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":40},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"632ade713a7ace5e1917b3e13bbe4368b99ed7516742c636fee71cb342dcea2a"},"summary":"A page learns who its viewer is from the site once: a rename, a sign-in or a change of rights shows in user.* only from the next document","supersedes":"9be550fdbf1d2060a46ba37629ba482ba0b8cc7b86809d74f710212b11d706e7","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:10:11.312221Z","id":"5279b27ffe7ec4d013b7509849b696ecac229a4eb4be0a67f0b96a68b18a6a60","body":{"detail":"The site API serves whoami but no viewers' names (no /api/viewers on /_clax/api/), so userLocals answers profiles with the viewer's own name and \"\" for every other ID, and search with [], unless a framing Clax shell serves user (then web/shell/src/caps/user.ts looks them up). A top-level page that shows room peers or document authors by name shows them unnamed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":422},"end":{"line":488},"content_hash":"f0681012a59f53638565dc7b484158ebc0329a9f596668d76fb7ce4017cb2031"},"suggested_fix":"A /_clax/api/viewers?ids= route answering the names the caller's level may see, for the bridge to call in place of the shell.","summary":"user.profiles and user.search on a page opened directly on its site name only the viewer and find no one","supersedes":"1b8d30f5aaa319a37749f6243a08c0c2e05eebf3f6a5d46fe39ffd1f2f929cca","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/bridge/src/caps/origin.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:10:11.472943Z","id":"b6ea158fe1fbf8ee350735e7dc63c6c70d3548ca67178e59ec1cd56c08740df9","body":{"detail":"repoll uses UNWATCHED_POLL_MS whenever sources.size > 0, so in a framed view a single read subscription makes tick() refetch every subscription, the page's own included, though the shell's db.watch reports those. main delivered the source's changes over the shell's stream topic docs:<B>?reader=<A>; nothing subscribes it now (crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs Topic::DocsRead, Hub::check_reads; crates/clax-http/src/state.rs start_listeners; crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs update). Options: (a) push through A's site: a change channel on A's site host carrying B's doc events while the site caller may read B (site_api.rs read_source) and A may read B (db_caller::reads_now), closed or narrowed on Event::Access as the site room socket is; on the Worker it needs a socket kind whose attachment keeps the watched sources and site credentials for reopen (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs reopen, opened), and it would also give a top-level page its own documents' changes (thread c955cd98). Then remove the public-host topic. (b) the framing shell subscribes docs:<B>?reader=<A> on its own stream and relays db/changed with the source, as main did: framed views only, a few dozen lines in web/shell/src/caps/db.ts and the bridge; keep the topic and check there that the stream's caller may read A and B. web/e2e/db-artifact.spec.ts brings the refetch about with a visibilitychange instead of waiting out a poll.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":246},"end":{"line":256},"content_hash":"190c38609e6bde716164c39890f5a4c8346b0c5030d7aa46e03ec65d2f995397"},"summary":"db.artifact(id) subscriptions poll the page's own site (5 s rising to 30 s), and while one is held every subscription of the view polls too; main pushed the source's changes live","tags":["status:needs-decision","site-origins","perf","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
